 "source": {
  "citation": "B. Leissner, Strahluntersuchungen am TESLA Linearbeschleuniger, Diplomarbeit, RWTH Aachen, PITHA 99/4 (1998), Sec. 7.1, Fig. 7.5 (thesis p. 72)",
  "zotero_item": "MDUGLCM5",
  "verified": "2026-11-14",
  "method": "Curve vertices read from the thesis PDF's vector paths (PDF page 74; pdftocairo -svg, path transform applied), not from a raster. Axes calibrated on the tick marks: time from the -5 and 25 ps frame ticks (324.0 units per 5 ps, t=0 at x=2289), ordinate from the 0 and 1.0 ticks (y=6027 and 7206). Colors per legend: blue dashed 154 GHz, red dash-dot 77 GHz, green solid 51 GHz. All vertices kept; duplicates at dash joins removed.",
  "text_values_note": "Sec. 7.1 text quotes RMS 2.12, 2.48, 2.75 ps for these reconstructions; the positive-lobe RMS of the Fig. 7.5 curves is 2.04, 2.17, 2.31 ps (same convention: stop at the first negative value). 2.48 ps equals the lobe RMS of Fig. 7.3, a different 77 GHz reconstruction whose settings are not stated; the text values are not used."
 },
